                                               {takeoff,landing}

Fly the 737-800 through takeoff or landing with a fly brain.

    python -m flight_simulator.takeoff_landing takeoff --brain connectome
    python -m flight_simulator.takeoff_landing landing --brain connectome
    python -m flight_simulator.takeoff_landing takeoff --brain standin --fault-at-kt 100   # rejected takeoff
    python -m flight_simulator.takeoff_landing landing --brain connectome --silence looming  # lesion control

Two configured brains on one connectome (docs/TAKEOFF_LANDING_PLAN.md):
the Takeoff fly is a *standing* fly (looming -> jump = rotation), the Landing
fly is a *flying* fly (looming -> DNp07 leg extension = flare).

--brain connectome runs the real FlyWire 783 LIF model (needs requirements-brain.txt
and `python -m flight_simulator.download_data`). --brain standin is a
deterministic lookup of the measured probe table, labelled as NOT a fly brain,
for fast offline runs and tests.

Exit status: 0 = success criteria met, 2 = failed (crash, tail strike, hard
landing, off the runway), 1 = configuration/runtime error.

positional arguments:
  {takeoff,landing}

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --brain {connectome,standin}
  --backend {demo,flightgear}
  --data DATA
  --seed SEED
  --no-calibrate        Skip the pre-flight adaptation trials that measure the
                        zero points
  --noise-seed NOISE_SEED
                        standin only: add the connectome's spike-count noise
                        (1-4 neurons per readout)
  --silence {sugar,bitter,looming,hs_left,hs_right,vs_left,vs_right,translational_flow,DNp01,DNp02,DNp04,DNp06,DNp11,DNp07,DNp10,DNp09,MDN,DNg02,DNa01_L,DNa01_R,DNa02_L,DNa02_R,DNp15_L,DNp15_R,DNp20_L,DNp20_R,DNp22_L,DNp22_R,MN9} [{sugar,bitter,looming,hs_left,hs_right,vs_left,vs_right,translational_flow,DNp01,DNp02,DNp04,DNp06,DNp11,DNp07,DNp10,DNp09,MDN,DNg02,DNa01_L,DNa01_R,DNa02_L,DNa02_R,DNp15_L,DNp15_R,DNp20_L,DNp20_R,DNp22_L,DNp22_R,MN9} ...]
                        Lesion control: cut the outgoing synapses of these
                        groups
  --period PERIOD       Seconds of sim time between brain trials
  --seconds SECONDS
  --fault-at-kt FAULT_AT_KT
                        Takeoff: inject a reject condition at this speed
  --offset-m OFFSET_M   Initial centerline offset (demo)
  --yaw-drift YAW_DRIFT
                        Takeoff ground yaw disturbance, rad/s (demo)
  --start-speed-kt START_SPEED_KT
                        Landing: initial approach speed (demo)
  --high-ft HIGH_FT     Landing: start this far above the glideslope (demo)
  --runway LAT LON HDG  FlightGear: runway threshold/brake-release point and
                        true heading
  --final-nm FINAL_NM   FlightGear landing without --runway: start distance
                        before the threshold, nm
  --approach-throttle APPROACH_THROTTLE
                        FlightGear landing: approach power
  --telemetry-port TELEMETRY_PORT
  --control-port CONTROL_PORT
  --vision-port VISION_PORT
                        Synthetic fly-view UDP port; 0 disables display stream
  --vision-obstacles VISION_OBSTACLES
                        Known obstacles JSON in runway coordinates:
                        east=right, north=along; heights above runway
  --log LOG             CSV of every sim step, incl. sensory inputs and DN
                        rates
  --body-port BODY_PORT
                        UDP port of the live 3D fly window
  --no-fly-body         Do not stream to the 3D fly window
  --smooth              Accepted for old commands, no effect: FlightGear runs
                        are always real time (1x, no pause per brain trial)
  --no-cockpit-fly      Do not animate the fly pilot in the 737 cockpit
  --plot PLOT           PNG of sugar input, brain activity, altitude and
                        airspeed (needs matplotlib)
